Mwahhaahaha... Actually, the whole point is that is wouldn't. A truly
evil game like Nethack doesn't always give you a way to get to the
level above/below any time you feel like it (c.f. the Rogue quest.)
Wouldn't it be wonderful for the benighted adventurer fleeing an
Olog-hai to suddenly discover that not only has the staircase to the
level above moved to the other side of the dungeon, it now only leads
*down*, where there happens to be a pack of soldier ants waiting for
the next unwary victim... (Of course, in 2n turns it has a chance of
reverting, but that might be too long in certain circumstances.)

If you really need to get to another level quickly...well, that's what
cursed scrolls of teleportation are for. Or wands of digging. Or
potions of gain level. This is Nethack, after all -- not for the faint
of heart.

